  "ai_summary": "IT consultancy stocks are collapsing (-12.58% in 30 days, -24.44% YoY), pricing in AI automation for outsourced work. Yet, developer hiring intent remains resilient: the Indeed index rose 4.25% recently and 23.85% YoY. Big Tech headcounts show no systemic AI labor cuts (Meta's steep YoY drop has flatlined over 30 days), and Anthropic's open roles grew (+26 recently). Devs aren't cooked outside low-value IT. Asking if devs are cooked because Infosys stock dropped is like asking if gourmet chefs are finished because microwave burritos went on sale.",
